# The prolate spheroidal wave function of order zero on the host (D266):
# psi, its eigenvalue, C0 = int_0^1 psi, and chi_hat against the eigenfunction
# of the integral operator by Gauss-Legendre in mpmath at 40 digits
# (scripts/benchmarks/prolate-ewald/pswf_reference.py), to 1e-12 of psi(0);
# the bandwidths of Table 2 of Liang et al. (2026) to their printed digits;
# the mesh error estimate of the B-spline window (D444)
# against scripts/benchmarks/prolate-ewald/spline_grid.py functional.
# RUN: mdir-prolate-test > %t
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t
# CHECK-NOT: FAIL
# CHECK: c 9.5392 lambda
# CHECK: c 14.4712 lambda
# CHECK: epsilon 1e-05 bandwidth 14.471
# CHECK: spline spectrum: {{.*}} ok
# CHECK-COUNT-5: spline mesh error {{.*}} ok
# CHECK: spline mesh error 160x160x160 on 1 and 4 threads: {{.*}} ok
# CHECK: series of (1 - Phi)/(1 - x) at epsilon 1e-05: 23 terms, {{.*}} ok
# CHECK: C3 cutoff N=8 at c 9.5392: {{.*}} ok
# CHECK: C3 cutoff N=8 at c 14.471: {{.*}} ok
# CHECK: 0 failures
